✅ Q17 — Find All Strings That Have the Same Length as the Longest String

🎗️ 17.1 Problem Statement

You are given a List<String> containing strings of different lengths.
Using Java Streams, find all strings whose length is equal to the maximum string length.

Your solution should:

👉 Use the Stream API.
🔴 Return the result as a List<String>.
🔴 Preserve the original encounter order.
🔴 Correctly handle duplicate strings.
🔴 Correctly handle empty strings.
🔴 Correctly handle an empty list.
🔴 Do not sort the list unnecessarily.

🎗️ 17.2 Input / Output

👉 Input List

Use this exact list in your Java program:
List<String> words = Arrays.asList("Java","Spring","Microservices","Docker","Kubernetes","Architecture","API");

👉 Expected Output : [Microservices, Architecture]

Because:

Java           → 4
Spring         → 6
Microservice  → 12  ✅
Docker         → 6
Kubernetes     → 10
Architecture   → 12 ✅
API            → 3

⚠️ Correction: With the above input, only Microservices has the maximum length.
So the actual expected output is : [Microservices,Architecture]

To properly practice the "all maximum-length elements" requirement, use this input instead:
List<String> words = Arrays.asList("Java","Spring","Microservices","Docker","Kubernetes","Architecture","API");

👉 Expected Output : [Microservices, Architecture] Both have length 12.

🎗️ 17.3 Your Task

Write the Java Stream solution.
You can provide:

🔴 Your primary approach
🔴 Any alternative approaches — Streams only
🔴 How you handle an empty list
🔴 How you preserve encounter order
🔴 How you handle duplicate maximum-length strings
🔴 Time and space complexity, if you want to attempt those too.